+## Persistence and MV3 recovery
+
+Background snapshots are written through one serialized queue. Every snapshot
+has `stateRevision` and `persistenceGeneration`; older asynchronous writes
+cannot overwrite a newer committed state. Stop/cancel advances the generation
+and writes a run tombstone, preventing a suspended worker write from reviving a
+terminated run.
+
+On an ordinary MV3 wake, `TabMapManager` is loaded first, then the latest valid
+run snapshot. Reconciliation validates live provider tabs, projects bindings
+back into compatibility fields and derives model/pipeline statuses from their
+canonical state. Volatile timers and DOM observations are never treated as
+persisted truth.
